  {
    "title": "s before a vowel sounds like “z”",
    "body": "Before a vowel, s is a buzzing “z”: sie, also, Sohn. In southern Germany, Austria and Switzerland it is often a plain “s”.",
    "pattern": "(?<!\\p{L})s(?=[aeiouäöüy])|(?<=[aeiouäöüylrnm])s(?=[aeiouäöüy])",
    "examples": [
