  {
    "title": "ss and ß are a sharp “s”",
    "body": "Both are the sharp “s” of “miss”, never “z”. ß comes after long vowels and ei, au, eu, while ss comes after short vowels, so they also tell you the vowel length.",
    "pattern": "ss|ß",
    "examples": [
      {
        "word": "groß",
        "say": "grohs",
