  {
    "title": "v usually sounds like “f”",
    "body": "In German words v is “f”: Vater, viel, von. In words from Latin or French it is “v”: November, Universität, Video, Klavier.",
    "pattern": "v",
    "examples": [
      {
        "word": "der Vater",
        "say": "dare FAH-tuh",
        "en": "father"
      },
      {
        "word": "von",
        "say": "fon",
        "en": "from, of"
      },
