        "word": "voll",
        "say": "fol",
        "en": "full"
      },
      {
        "word": "der November",
        "say": "dare no-VEM-buh",
        "en": "November"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "ng is one sound, as in “singer”",
    "body": "ng is the single sound of “singer”, with no g after it as in “finger”; nk is “ngk” as in “think”. When n and g belong to different word parts, both are said: an-ge-kommen.",
    "pattern": "(?<!(?<!\\p{L})(?:a|ei|hi|u))ng|(?<!\\p{L})angst",
    "examples": [
      {
        "word": "lang",
        "say": "lahng",
        "en": "long"
      },
      {
