        "say": "dee TSYE-toong",
        "en": "newspaper"
      },
      {
        "word": "der Finger",
        "say": "dare FING-uh",
        "en": "finger"
      },
      {
        "word": "singen",
        "say": "ZING-uhn",
        "en": "to sing"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "sp and st at the start of a word are “shp”, “sht”",
    "body": "At the start of a word or word part, sp and st are said “shp” and “sht”. Inside or at the end of a word they are a plain “sp” and “st”: Fenster, ist, gestern.",
    "pattern": "(?<!\\p{L})(?:ver)?s[pt]",
    "examples": [
      {
        "word": "sprechen",
        "say": "SHPREKH-uhn",
        "en": "to speak"
