      },
      {
        "word": "die Straße",
        "say": "dee SHTRAH-suh",
        "en": "street"
      },
      {
        "word": "spät",
        "say": "shpayt",
        "en": "late"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "ä sounds like the German e",
    "body": "ä is said like e: short ä is the “e” of “bed”; long ä is a long open “eh”, which many speakers say like long e, “ay”.",
    "pattern": "ä(?!u)",
    "examples": [
      {
