  {
    "title": "Loanwords often stress the end: -ieren, -tät, -ei",
    "body": "Many words from French, Latin or English stress a late syllable: verbs in -ieren stress the ie, nouns in -tät and -ei stress that ending. Musik, Büro and Café also stress the last syllable.",
    "pattern": "(?<=\\p{L}{3})(?<!e)ier(?=en|t|e|st)|tät|(?<=\\p{L}{4})ei(?!\\p{L})",
    "examples": [
      {
        "word": "studieren",
        "say": "shtoo-DEE-ruhn",
